What is a Priority Queue?
---------------------------
A Priority Queue (PQ) is a special type of queue where elements are removed based on priority, not on insertion order.
Java Priority Queue
''Java's PriorityQueue is Min Heap by default.''
int a[] = {2,12,34,89,2,4,3,90};
        PriorityQueue<Integer>pq = new PriorityQueue<>();
        for(int n:a){
            pq.add(n);
        }
         while(!pq.isEmpty()){
            System.out.println(pq.poll());
        }
2 2 3 4 12 34 89 90 
